  "worked_solution": "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-7+5}{2},\\frac{2+(-6)}{2}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{2},-\\frac{4}{2}) \\\\  & =(-1,-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(-1,-2)$ and a point on the circle, such as $(5,-6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-1-5)}^{2}+{(-2-(-6))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,-2),$ and its radius is $2\\sqrt{13}.$",
